        "title": "Robotics - AI and Learning-Based Robotics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The MDP formulation for robotics (S: robot state, A: joint torques, R: task completion) is structurally identical to RL for infrastructure optimization — VM placement, autoscale policy, and workload scheduling all use the same (S: resource state, A: placement/scaling decision, R: cost + SLA satisfaction) MDP structure. The abstraction is universal; the physics (joint dynamics vs. request latency) determines the transition function P(s'|s,a)."
